--
--   Description
--
-- This test is intended to cover the transmit functionality of the
-- GEM in gigabit operation when using the TBI (PCS layer) interface.
-- Full duplex operation is used throughout this test case. Input data
-- to the MAC is supplied via the external fifo interface.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- · Ensure the link status interrupt indicates a good link.
--  
-- . Ensure the PCS correctly transmits all 256 valid data code groups
--   with both even and odd disparity.
--
-- · Ensure an error (tx_err) is correctly propagated through the MAC and PCS.
--  
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
--
-- The auto-negotiation function is disabled (using bit-7 of the PCS
-- Control Register) prior to selecting PCS. The PCS is selected
-- by setting the MAC into Gigabit mode and setting PCS enable in the
-- MAC network configuration register.
--
-- Wait for the link status interrupt.
--
-- SINGLE FRAME - FRAME 1.
--
-- Generate a single frame with all 256 valid code groups repeated twice, the
-- first with odd disparity and the second with even disparity. The data code
-- groups '00' and '03' are used to maintain/reverse the current disparity.
--
-- Generate a single frame with an error received from the external fifo
-- interface.
--
-- Check the statistics registers.
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


